  "unresolved": [
    {
      "key": "STYLE",
      "config": [
        "IK_VAL_STYLE",
        "IK_PARITY_STYLE"
      ],
      "status": "unresolved \u2014 the parity test skips",
      "note": "fast-neural-style `mosaic.pth` is no longer served: download.pytorch.org/models/fast_neural_style/{mosaic.pth,saved_models.zip}, the S3 path, and the web.archive copy all 403/404 as of 2026-08-19, and the only HF hit is an ExecuTorch .pte this loader cannot read. A SEEDED checkpoint from the reference `transformer_net.py` was tried and REJECTED: the network is trained to emit 0...255, so with random weights its output is near-zero noise (range about +-1.5 before the divide by 255) and the cosine measures the port's noise floor rather than the model \u2014 it scored 0.68, which looks like a failure and means nothing. Same trap as matting on a synthetic plate. The recorded 0.9999926 was measured on the official checkpoint; re-running it needs that file to reappear or a mirror to be found."
    }
  ],
  "sources": {
